---

Third-party components:

Rust libraries (built into the recording program)
  Each is listed with its version and licence in capture/THIRD-PARTY.md, which is made by
  capture/tools/check_rules.py and checked on every change. All are on the allowed licence list
  (Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD, ISC, Zlib, Unlicense, CC0 and similar).

JavaScript packages (bundled into the app window)
  @tauri-apps/api, @tauri-apps/plugin-dialog and @tauri-apps/plugin-opener: MIT OR Apache-2.0,
  from the Tauri project. They are the only JavaScript libraries in the page.

Rust libraries of the app window (app/src-tauri, the Tauri framework and what it uses)
  259 libraries for Windows, checked by app/tools/check_app_licences.py. All but five are on the allowed
  licence list. The five are under the Mozilla Public License 2.0, which applies to the files of those
  libraries and not to this program: cssparser, cssparser-macros, dtoa-short, option-ext and selectors.
  The project owner accepted them on 2026-10-24. They come in through Tauri, are used unmodified, and their
  source is published on crates.io. The condition of the acceptance: if any of those files is ever changed
  here, the changed files must be published under the MPL-2.0, and this notice updated. The full list with
  versions and licences is made by the check before a release is built.

The application icon
  app/branding/OpenStageRecorder.svg is the picture of a film camera that the project owner supplied for this
  app (supplied under the file name OpenRecorder.svg; only the file name and the title inside the file were
  changed, not the picture). It is released under Apache-2.0 with the rest of the project. The icon files in
  app/src-tauri/icons and app/web/icon.svg are made from it.

Windows' own capture and encoding services
  Screen and window capture, sound capture and MP4 encoding use services that Windows already
  provides. Nothing from them is included in this repository. FFmpeg is not used.

Any further bundled library, font, icon or model is listed here with its licence before it ships.
Open weights are not automatically open source: check each one.
